From: Sebastian Matkovich <sebastian.matkovich@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 11:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm6115-pro1x: a deep-buffer playback front
 end (MultiMedia4)

Music played through MultiMedia1 wakes the CPU once per period: every
period is one ASM write to the ADSP and one WRITE_DONE back, and the
sound server refills it. PulseAudio cannot use timer-based scheduling on
q6asm-dai (it sets SNDRV_PCM_INFO_BATCH, and PulseAudio turns tsched off
for batch devices), so the period it opens with (about 20 ms) is the
wake-up interval for everything, a notification sound as well as an hour
of music.

A second playback front end lets the sound server keep two sinks: the
UCM one on MultiMedia1 with short periods for interactive sounds, and a
music sink with periods of up to 640 ms (q6asm-dai's limit after the
next patch). The ADSP mixes both sessions into the codec's
RX_CODEC_DMA_RX_0 port (one COPP, two sessions in its matrix map), so the
UCM profile's speaker, headphone and earpiece paths serve both.

MultiMedia2 and MultiMedia3 are taken by capture (the microphones, the
FM receiver), and a front end is one ASM session that its playback and
capture streams would share, so the new one is MultiMedia4, playback
only. Its DAI link is the last one: the card numbers its PCMs by link
order, back ends included, so the existing ones (VoiceMMode1 is 5) keep
their numbers and MultiMedia4 is hw:<card>,8. Like MultiMedia1 it opens
only while a route ("RX_CODEC_DMA_RX_0 Audio Mixer MultiMedia4") is on.

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115-fxtec-pro1x.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115-fxtec-pro1x.dts
index 91755b757a..58de6cfbbb 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115-fxtec-pro1x.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115-fxtec-pro1x.dts
@@ -567,6 +567,20 @@ platform {
 				sound-dai = <&q6routing>;
 			};
 		};
+
+		/*
+		 * A second playback front end for music with large periods (a
+		 * deep buffer): the DSP mixes it with MultiMedia1 on
+		 * RX_CODEC_DMA_RX_0. Last, so that the PCM numbers of the links
+		 * above stay as they were (it is hw:<card>,8).
+		 */
+		mm4-dai-link {
+			link-name = "MultiMedia4";
+
+			cpu {
+				sound-dai = <&q6asmdai MSM_FRONTEND_DAI_MULTIMEDIA4>;
+			};
+		};
 	};
 
 	ts_i2c: i2c-touchscreen {
@@ -1538,6 +1552,18 @@ dai@1 {
 	};
 };
 
+/*
+ * MultiMedia4, the deep-buffer front end (mm4-dai-link): playback only.
+ * Each front end is one ASM session, which its playback and capture
+ * streams would share.
+ */
+&q6asmdai {
+	dai@3 {
+		reg = <MSM_FRONTEND_DAI_MULTIMEDIA4>;
+		direction = <Q6ASM_DAI_RX>;
+	};
+};
+
 &cci {
 	status = "okay";
 };
